  "details": "Right now we can access the old bone position from last frame (?) during `Update()` and for the current frame during `PostLateUpdate()`.\n\nWhen we try accessing the bone position outside of this frame timing, for example in `LateUpdate()`, we get access to some weird in-between IK data (?) that is completely useless to us. \n\nThe Udon VM should always return the cached bone positions from the last time that IK calculations finished, so it is never wrong.\n\nThe attached GIF shows the hand bone position during `LateUpdate()` in red, and during `PostLateUpdate()` in green. As you can see, we don't get anything usable during `LateUpdate()` and possibly also during a lot of other events.",
